1. Why You Are Doing This & How It Helps DevOps Teams Daily

In real-world DevOps, SRE, and Production Support roles, engineers rarely run isolated commands. When an alert fires at 2:00 AM, an on-call engineer must rapidly:
1. Verify host health and dependencies (uname, command -v, which, type, systemctl) before running recovery scripts.
2. Safely isolate and back up corrupted configs or noisy logs (pwd, cd, ls, cp, file, rm) without causing data loss.
3. Extract, sanitize, and summarize failure patterns (grep, cut, tr, sed, awk, journalctl) from massive log streams to find root causes in seconds rather than hours.
By automating this entire workflow into a single Bash triage toolkit, you prove to recruiters and hiring managers that you don't just memorize syntax—you solve operational bottlenecks.

